[{"id":758,"name":"AlphaRAR.qm_increments_resp","kind":"Lemma","keyword":"lemma","module":"AlphaRAR.YDK2026.ResponseIncrement","package":"AlphaRAR","isProp":true,"hashes":{"meaning":"86f3727a3525a3cd","local":"c2c884895476c0ae","content":"25a337a587f6b788"},"doc":"**The response-martingale increment maxima are `o_p(1)` and `o_p(√n)`**, the probabilistic core\nof the increment control for `Q` used in Appendix A of the paper. For each window the deterministic\nincrement control is `AlphaRAR.norm_increment_le_vmaxSeq_wmaxSeq`. ","statement":{"binders":[{"explicit":false,"name":"Ω","role":"type","type":"Type u_1"},{"explicit":false,"name":"𝓐","role":"type","type":"Type u_2"},{"explicit":false,"name":"mΩ","role":"instance","type":"MeasurableSpace Ω"},{"explicit":false,"name":"m𝓐","role":"instance","type":"MeasurableSpace 𝓐"},{"explicit":false,"name":"","role":"instance","type":"MeasurableSingletonClass 𝓐"},{"explicit":false,"name":"","role":"instance","type":"Fintype 𝓐"},{"explicit":false,"name":"ν","role":"variable","type":"ProbabilityTheory.Kernel 𝓐 ℝ"},{"explicit":false,"name":"","role":"instance","type":"ProbabilityTheory.IsMarkovKernel ν"},{"explicit":false,"name":"P","role":"variable","type":"MeasureTheory.Measure Ω"},{"explicit":false,"name":"","role":"instance","type":"MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure P"},{"explicit":false,"name":"O","role":"variable","type":"ℕ → Ω → Unit"},{"explicit":false,"name":"A","role":"variable","type":"ℕ → Ω → 𝓐"},{"explicit":false,"name":"Y","role":"variable","type":"ℕ → Ω → ℝ"},{"explicit":false,"name":"alg","role":"variable","type":"Learning.Algorithm Unit 𝓐 ℝ"},{"explicit":true,"name":"h","role":"hypothesis","type":"Learning.IsAlgEnvSeq O A Y alg (Learning.stationaryEnv ν) P"},{"explicit":true,"name":"hνk","role":"hypothesis","type":"∀ (a : 𝓐), MeasureTheory.MemLp id 2 (ν a)"}],"conclusion":"IsLittleOpOne P (vmaxSeq fun k => respMart ν A Y k) ∧\n  IsLittleOpOne P fun n ω => wmaxSeq (fun k => respMart ν A Y k) n ω / √↑n","decl":"AlphaRAR.qm_increments_resp"},"code":"/-- **The response-martingale increment maxima are `o_p(1)` and `o_p(√n)`**, the probabilistic core\nof the increment control for `Q` used in Appendix A of the paper. For each window the deterministic\nincrement control is `AlphaRAR.norm_increment_le_vmaxSeq_wmaxSeq`. -/\nlemma qm_increments_resp (h : IsAlgEnvSeq O A Y alg (stationaryEnv ν) P)\n    (hνk : ∀ a, MemLp id 2 (ν a)) :\n    IsLittleOpOne P (vmaxSeq (fun k ↦ respMart ν A Y k)) ∧\n      IsLittleOpOne P\n        (fun n ω ↦ wmaxSeq (fun k ↦ respMart ν A Y k) n ω / √n)","proof":":= by\n  have hY2 : ∀ n, MemLp (Y n) 2 P := fun n ↦ h.memLp_feedback hνk n\n  set ℱ := h.filtrationAction with hℱdef\n  have hint : ∀ n, Integrable (Y n) P := fun n ↦ (hY2 n).integrable one_le_two\n  have hMfam : ∀ k, Martingale (respMart ν A Y k) ℱ P := fun k ↦ martingale_respMart h hint k\n  have hM2fam : ∀ k n, MemLp (respMart ν A Y k n) 2 P :=\n    fun k n ↦ memLp_respMart h hY2 k n\n  have hcent2 : ∀ k n, Integrable (fun ω ↦ (Y n ω - ν.means k) ^ 2) P :=\n    fun k n ↦ ((hY2 n).sub (memLp_const _)).integrable_sq\n  have harmnn : ∀ k, 0 ≤ Var[id; ν k] := fun k ↦ variance_nonneg _ _\n  have hC₀ : 0 ≤ ∑ k, Var[id; ν k] := Finset.sum_nonneg (fun k _ ↦ harmnn k)\n  have hincfam : ∀ k n, ∫ ω, (respMart ν A Y k (n + 1) ω - respMart ν A Y k n ω) ^ 2 ∂P\n      ≤ ∑ k, Var[id; ν k] := fun k n ↦ (integral_respMart_increment_sq_le h k n hνk).trans\n    (Finset.single_le_sum (fun k' _ ↦ harmnn k') (Finset.mem_univ k))\n  exact ⟨isLittleOpOne_vmaxSeq (M := fun k ↦ respMart ν A Y k)\n      hMfam hM2fam hC₀ hincfam,\n    isLittleOpOne_wmaxSeq_div_sqrt (M := fun k ↦ respMart ν A Y k)\n      hMfam hM2fam hC₀ hincfam⟩","source":{"path":"AlphaRAR/YDK2026/ResponseIncrement.lean","start":38,"end":62,"url":"https://github.com/RemyDegenne/alpha-rar/blob/e7164a80baea3f4f65e108de31d2d561dd35e350/AlphaRAR/YDK2026/ResponseIncrement.lean#L38-L62"},"deps":[250,257,356,676],"outside":[],"external":[["AddCommMonoidWithOne.toAddM